    15	    /// @dev Planned swap input for maxAmount, in collateral token precision;
    16	    ///      the scaling basis callbacks use to pro-rate the encoded
    17	    ///      amountOutMinimum.
    18	    function plannedTakeAmount(IERC20Pool pool, uint256 maxAmount) internal view returns (uint256 plannedAmountIn) {
    19	        plannedAmountIn = maxAmount / pool.collateralScale();
    20	        require(plannedAmountIn > 0, "Zero planned amount");
    21	    }
    22	
    23	    /// @dev Pro-rates the full-size output floor to the collateral Ajna
    24	    ///      actually sent. Enforcing the unscaled floor would reject valid
    25	    ///      debt-constrained partial fills; rounding up preserves the quoted
    26	    ///      per-unit floor at any fill size, and quoteAmountDue remains a
    27	    ///      separate repayment backstop in each taker.
    28	    /// @dev MEV note: the keeper quotes fullSizeAmountOutMinimum with slippage
    29	    ///      against the FULL planned size. A partial fill has less price impact,
    30	    ///      so this linear pro-rate is a LOOSE (lower) floor than the partial
    31	    ///      fill could achieve, widening the sandwich window on a public-mempool
    32	    ///      take. This is bounded below by quoteAmountDue (the auction is always
    33	    ///      repaid; no principal loss) and is mitigated operationally by the
    34	    ///      keeper's private-RPC / relay submission. Tightening on-chain would
    35	    ///      require the partial-fill spot price, which is not available in the
    36	    ///      callback.
    37	    function scaleAmountOutMinimum(
    38	        uint256 fullSizeAmountOutMinimum,
    39	        uint256 actualAmountIn,
    40	        uint256 plannedAmountIn
    41	    ) internal pure returns (uint256) {
    42	        if (actualAmountIn == plannedAmountIn) return fullSizeAmountOutMinimum;
    43	        return Math.mulDiv(fullSizeAmountOutMinimum, actualAmountIn, plannedAmountIn, Math.Rounding.Up);
    44	    }
